SOLUTION
Here’s the quickest way to complete it in Jenkins:

Open Jenkins
Click Jenkins in the top bar.
Log in:
Username: admin
Password: Adm!n321
Create the Apache folder
From the Jenkins dashboard, click New Item.
Enter:
Apache
Select Folder.
Click OK.
Click Save if prompted.
Move httpd-php into Apache
Open the existing httpd-php job.
Click Move in the left-side menu.
Select the destination folder:
Apache
Confirm the move.
Move services into Apache
Return to the Jenkins dashboard.
Open services.
Click Move.
Select:
Apache
Confirm.

Verify

Go back to the Jenkins dashboard.
Open Apache.
You should see:
httpd-php
services

The final structure should be:

Jenkins
└── Apache
    ├── httpd-php
    └── services
If “Move” is not available

You may need the Folders plugin. Go to:

Manage Jenkins → Plugins → Available plugins

Search for Folders, install it, and select Restart Jenkins when installation is complete and no jobs are running if Jenkins requests a restart.

After Jenkins comes back, refresh the browser and repeat the steps above.

